local-end-1.0.bin: input that makes the local-end oracle fire on code that builds path.local from c->local (1.0, limiti-su-quic).
With the migration (branch migrazione-su-limiti) it passes: run it alone with `bin/quic-conn -runs=1 known/local-end-1.0.bin`.
age-after-decreed-login.bin: crash-5e4ce06f (rootside-completo d283a02b, 25 Oct 2026): the harness decreed a state past the credentials on an unlogged connection; with transport.c without the login seen in transport_expired() (8d5629f3) the age close hit it.  Fixed in the harness (op_wt logs in by transport_verdict first): it passes now, run it alone with bin/quic-conn -runs=1 known/age-after-decreed-login.bin.
age-decreed-login-write-fail.bin: the same input with wt_write_fail on the decreed connection: transport_write() inside the verdict reaps it, so the harness must not touch `c` after transport_verdict() (heap-use-after-free, review of 82e87313).  Run it alone with bin/quic-conn -runs=1 known/age-decreed-login-write-fail.bin.
stateless-reset-no-source.bin: crash-7bea7aa0 of verifica-rami on finale (3fc45b85, 25 Oct 2026): op 13 (BURST) on an IPv6 transport, a Stateless Reset for an unknown connection id. The oracle "a packet left without its source address" fired because the harness left T->bound_any false (T is made by hand, not by transport_open_fd): a defect of the HARNESS since pktinfo (52c3b599) gated the control message on bound_any, not of the product. It passes with T->bound_any = true.
